KP_BOOK_CHAPTER("en","scenare","<h1 id=\"scenare\"><span class=\"ch-label\">Chapter 32</span>Story scenarios: you decide</h1>\n<p>Knowing what to do and doing it under pressure are two different things. In these six stories you find yourself in a crisis and make a decision at every step. Some choices move you safely forward; others have consequences. Every risky decision comes with a tip and a link to the chapter where you can learn more. The stories are fictional, but the situations and mistakes in them happen again and again in real crises.</p>\n<h2 id=\"scenare-ako\">How to play</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>On the website and in the app</strong>, press <strong>▶ Play the story</strong> next to a story. The choices appear one by one, and at the end you see your result, tips to review and a list of things worth preparing.</li>\n<li><strong>On paper and in the PDF</strong>, each story is divided into numbered sections (§). Start at the section given for the story and turn to the next number according to your choice. The sections are deliberately shuffled so you cannot see ahead how a choice turns out.</li>\n<li>A section marked <strong>✔</strong> means a good decision; <strong>✖</strong> means a risky one. At the end, count the ✔ marks on your path.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"tip\">\n<p>Play together with your family or children – everyone votes on what they would do, then you read the outcome together. It is a quick, low-pressure way to rehearse your family plan.</p>\n</div>\n<section class=\"scenario\" data-scenario=\"blackout\">\n<h2 id=\"scenar-blackout\">🔦 Winter blackout in a tower block</h2>\n<p class=\"sc-setting\">January, −8 °C outside. You live with your family in a 6th-floor flat. It is 6 pm and the lights go out everywhere.</p>\n<div class=\"sc-player no-print\" data-player=\"blackout\"></div>\n<div class=\"gamebook\" data-gamebook=\"blackout\">\n<p class=\"gb-start\">📖 Paper gamebook (numbered sections): The story starts at <a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-start\">§1</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-start\"></span>)</span>.</p>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-blackout-start\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§1</p><p>It is 6 pm, freezing outside, and the whole flat goes dark. The lift stops and the fridge falls silent. From the window you can see the neighbouring blocks are dark too.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-radio\">Switch on the battery radio to find out what is going on → turn to §19</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-radio\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-call112\">Call 112 and ask when the power will be back → turn to §11</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-call112\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-blackout-stay\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§2</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> The next night it is 11 °C indoors. The children are coughing and grandma is shivering. In the morning you set off for the school after all.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 When it falls below 12 °C at home and you have no safe heat source, move to relatives or a warming centre. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/mrazy/mrazy-vypadok\">→ Ch. 11 › When the heating fails<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"mrazy-vypadok\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-end\">Turn to §21</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-end\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-blackout-cold\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§3</p><p>It is 9 pm and the flat is down to 17 °C. The central heating has stopped because its pumps need electricity. How do you keep the family warm?</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-warm\">Everyone moves to the smallest room; you hang blankets over the windows and get out sleeping bags and hot-water bottles → turn to §17</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-warm\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-co\">Turn on the gas hob and oven to heat the flat → turn to §13</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-co\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-blackout-phonebad\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§4</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> By morning the phone and the power bank are both flat. Your family cannot reach you and you cannot check what is happening.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Save battery: power-saving mode, short texts, agreed times. Keep power banks charged in advance. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/varovanie/varovanie-spojenie\">→ Ch. 2 › Family communication in a crisis<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"varovanie-spojenie\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-neighbour\">Turn to §12</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-neighbour\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-blackout-helpok\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§5</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> The school is warm, with tea and chargers. The children play with others and Mrs Mary can finally rest.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-end\">Turn to §21</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-end\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-blackout-neighbourbad\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§6</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> In the evening you hear paramedics on the stairs. Mrs Mary was lying cold and confused in her freezing flat without food. Neighbours found her late.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 In a crisis neighbours are the first help. Check on older people and those living alone on the very first day. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/zranitelni/zranitelni-susedia\">→ Ch. 25 › Neighbours who need help<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"zranitelni-susedia\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-toilet\">Turn to §10</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-toilet\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-blackout-toiletok\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§7</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> There is enough water in the bath for flushing, and the drinking water lasts for drinking and cooking.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-help\">Turn to §15</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-help\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-blackout-toiletbad\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§8</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> The drinking water disappears fast. By evening you are down to the last bottle.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Keep drinking water for drinking and cooking. Use grey water or an emergency toilet for flushing. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/hygiena-psychika/hygiena-zachod\">→ Ch. 24 › Emergency toilet<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"hygiena-zachod\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-help\">Turn to §15</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-help\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-blackout-shop\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§9</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> The shop next door is closed; the other one has a long queue and takes cash only because the card terminals are down. By the time you get back, the tap is only dripping.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Pumps in apartment buildings stop soon after the power goes. Fill containers immediately and keep 3 days of water at home. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/zasoby/zasoby-voda\">→ Ch. 4 › Water – the most important supply<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"zasoby-voda\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-cold\">Turn to §3</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-cold\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-blackout-toilet\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§10</p><p>Day three. There is no running water and the toilet will not flush, but the sewer still works.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-toiletok\">Flush with bath water – pour a bucket into the bowl in one go → turn to §7</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-toiletok\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-toiletbad\">Flush with drinking water from the bottles → turn to §8</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-toiletbad\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-blackout-call112\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§11</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> The line is overloaded. When you get through, the operator politely asks you to keep it free for people whose lives are in danger. You have lost time and battery.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Call 112 only when a life is at risk. Get information from the radio and your municipality. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/varovanie/varovanie-112\">→ Ch. 2 › How to call the emergency line<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"varovanie-112\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-radio\">Turn to §19</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-radio\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-blackout-neighbour\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§12</p><p>The morning of day two. Mrs Mary on the 8th floor is 82 and lives alone. Nobody has seen her since yesterday.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-neighbourok\">Knock on her door and ask whether she needs anything → turn to §16</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-neighbourok\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-neighbourbad\">You do not want to disturb her – surely her family will look after her → turn to §6</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-neighbourbad\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-blackout-co\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§13</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> After an hour you and the children have headaches and grandma feels sick – signs of carbon monoxide poisoning! You switch off the cooker, open the windows and everyone gets fresh air. Luckily you noticed in time.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 A cooker, oven, barbecue or camping stove is not a heater. Have a CO alarm and keep the warmth in one room. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/mrazy/mrazy-vypadok\">→ Ch. 11 › When the heating fails<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"mrazy-vypadok\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-phone\">Turn to §20</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-phone\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-blackout-phoneok\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§14</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> Your contact person knows you are all right, and the battery will last several days.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-neighbour\">Turn to §12</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-neighbour\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-blackout-help\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§15</p><p>A municipal loudspeaker van announces a heated help point at the school with drinking water and phone charging. The flat is down to 12 °C.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-helpok\">Go there with your family and Mrs Mary, take medicines and documents, and leave a note on the door → turn to §5</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-helpok\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-stay\">Stay at home – you will manage somehow → turn to §2</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-stay\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-blackout-neighbourok\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§16</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> Mrs Mary is sitting in her coat in a cold flat with no way to heat food. You give her a hot-water bottle and hot tea, and agree she will spend the days in your warm room.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-toilet\">Turn to §10</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-toilet\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-blackout-warm\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§17</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> In the small room with blankets over the windows the temperature stays around 15 °C, and you can sleep in the sleeping bags. You fill the hot-water bottles with water heated on the camping stove by an open window.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-phone\">Turn to §20</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-phone\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-blackout-water\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§18</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> While the pressure lasted you filled about 80 litres – bottles for drinking, the bath for flushing. An hour later the water stops.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-cold\">Turn to §3</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-cold\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-blackout-radio\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§19</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> The radio reports a widespread outage across the region; repairs may take several days. Tap water is still running, but the pressure is dropping.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-water\">Fill bottles, pots and the bath with water right away → turn to §18</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-water\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-shop\">Go to the shop to buy water and candles → turn to §9</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-shop\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-blackout-phone\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§20</p><p>Your phone is at 40 % and the network is getting weaker. Family in another town are worried about you.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-phoneok\">Switch to power-saving mode, send a short text to your contact person and agree to switch on at 8 am and 8 pm → turn to §14</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-phoneok\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-blackout-phonebad\">Keep reading news and watching videos on social media to learn more → turn to §4</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-blackout-phonebad\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node end\" id=\"gb-blackout-end\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§21</p><p>On day four the power comes back. You switch appliances on one by one, check the food in the fridge and freezer, and replace everything you used up.</p><p class=\"gb-end\"><strong>The end.</strong> Count the ✔ marks on your path. Each ✖ shows something worth improving – its tip sends you to the right chapter.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"gb-prepare\"><p><strong>What to prepare in advance</strong></p><ul class=\"checklist\"><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> A battery radio and spare batteries</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> Water for 3 days – and fill the bath as soon as the power goes</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> Sleeping bags, blankets and hot-water bottles</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> Charged power banks</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> A carbon monoxide (CO) alarm</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> Contacts on paper and an arrangement with neighbours</li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"scenario\" data-scenario=\"flood\">\n<h2 id=\"scenar-flood\">🌊 Flood at night</h2>\n<p class=\"sc-setting\">You live in a house by a stream with your partner, two children and a dog. It has rained for two days and a flood warning is in force. It is 10 pm.</p>\n<div class=\"sc-player no-print\" data-player=\"flood\"></div>\n<div class=\"gamebook\" data-gamebook=\"flood\">\n<p class=\"gb-start\">📖 Paper gamebook (numbered sections): The story starts at <a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-start\">§22</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-start\"></span>)</span>.</p>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-flood-start\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§22</p><p>It is 10 pm, pouring with rain, and the stream behind the house is brown and fast, right up to the top of the bank. The municipality has declared flood alert level 2.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-prep\">Act now: move documents, medicines and valuables upstairs and park the car on higher ground → turn to §35</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-prep\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-sleep\">Go to bed – the water may still go down → turn to §34</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-sleep\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-flood-siren\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§23</p><p>At 2 am the flood siren sounds and a fire-brigade loudspeaker orders the street to evacuate.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-leave\">Take the grab bags and the dog and head straight for the car → turn to §29</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-leave\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-stay\">Stay – the house is solid and you will be safe upstairs → turn to §33</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-stay\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-flood-routeok\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§24</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> The hill road is slower but dry. By 3 am you are at grandma's.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-register\">Turn to §27</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-register\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-flood-regok\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§25</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> The municipality records your details and tells you when you can expect to return.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-return\">Turn to §28</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-return\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-flood-regbad\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§26</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> Firefighters search for your family among the missing and your neighbours are worried. Hours are lost that could have gone to others.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Always register, even if you are staying with relatives – it helps the search for missing people. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/evakuacia/evakuacia-prichod\">→ Ch. 7 › After you arrive<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"evakuacia-prichod\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-return\">Turn to §28</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-return\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-flood-register\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§27</p><p>In the morning the municipality asks all evacuees to register.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-regok\">Register by phone with the municipality, even though you are staying with grandma → turn to §25</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-regok\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-regbad\">Do not bother – you are safe after all → turn to §26</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-regbad\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-flood-return\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§28</p><p>Two days later the water recedes and you are allowed back. The house is knee-deep in mud.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-returnok\">Photograph and film everything first, then clean up. Have an electrician check the wiring → turn to §31</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-returnok\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-returnbad\">Throw out the ruined things straight away and switch the power back on to start drying → turn to §30</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-returnbad\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-flood-leave\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§29</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> Ten minutes later you are at the car. The street is still passable.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-route\">Turn to §36</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-route\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-flood-returnbad\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§30</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> The breaker trips immediately and a socket sparks. And the insurer asks for photos of ruined items you have already thrown away.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Document the damage first. Switch the power on only after a professional has checked it. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/komunita/komunita-poistenie\">→ Ch. 27 › Documentation and insurance<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"komunita-poistenie\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-end\">Turn to §37</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-end\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-flood-returnok\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§31</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> The insurer has all the evidence, and the electrician finds a short circuit in a flooded socket before it can start a fire.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-end\">Turn to §37</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-end\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-flood-underpass\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§32</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> The underpass is flooded. The water looks shallow, but halfway through the car loses grip and the engine dies. You climb out of the window and firefighters take you to an evacuation centre.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Never drive through moving water or flooded underpasses – 30 cm of water can carry a car away. Plan a route without bridges and underpasses. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/evakuacia/evakuacia-auto\">→ Ch. 7 › By car<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"evakuacia-auto\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-register\">Turn to §27</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-register\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-flood-stay\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§33</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> The water rises faster than you expected. In the morning firefighters take you from an upstairs window into a boat, and you have to leave the dog behind.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 When told to evacuate, leave immediately. People who wait often get trapped. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/principy/principy-rozhodnutia\">→ Ch. 1 › Three basic decisions: stay, shelter or leave<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"principy-rozhodnutia\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-register\">Turn to §27</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-register\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-flood-sleep\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§34</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> At 2 am the siren wakes you. There is water in the cellar and the car in the yard is standing in water up to the sills.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Act at once when a warning and alert level 2 are issued. Move the car, documents and valuables in time. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/povodne/povodne-stupa\">→ Ch. 8 › When the water is rising<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"povodne-stupa\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-siren\">Turn to §23</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-siren\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-flood-prep\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§35</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> By midnight the valuables are upstairs, the car is parked by the church on the hill, and you have sandbagged the ground-floor doors. You have turned off the gas and the main circuit breaker.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-siren\">Turn to §23</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-siren\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-flood-route\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§36</p><p>The shortest way to grandma's crosses the bridge over the stream and goes through a railway underpass. The other route is 6 km longer but runs along the hill.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-routeok\">Take the longer route along the hill → turn to §24</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-routeok\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-flood-underpass\">Take the shortest route – it is night and you are in a hurry → turn to §32</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-flood-underpass\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node end\" id=\"gb-flood-end\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§37</p><p>The clean-up takes weeks, with help from neighbours and volunteers. You restock the grab bags and note in your family plan what you will do differently next time.</p><p class=\"gb-end\"><strong>The end.</strong> Count the ✔ marks on your path. Each ✖ shows something worth improving – its tip sends you to the right chapter.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"gb-prepare\"><p><strong>What to prepare in advance</strong></p><ul class=\"checklist\"><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> A grab bag by the door</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> Documents in a waterproof pouch</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> Sandbags and plastic sheeting</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> An evacuation destination and two routes – at least one without bridges or underpasses</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> Photos of your belongings for the insurer</li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"scenario\" data-scenario=\"chemical\">\n<h2 id=\"scenar-chemical\">☣️ Siren and a smell of chlorine</h2>\n<p class=\"sc-setting\">Tuesday, 2 pm. You are at a playground with your 8-year-old son, 15 minutes from home. A water-treatment plant and an ice rink are nearby. Your daughter is at school.</p>\n<div class=\"sc-player no-print\" data-player=\"chemical\"></div>\n<div class=\"gamebook\" data-gamebook=\"chemical\">\n<p class=\"gb-start\">📖 Paper gamebook (numbered sections): The story starts at <a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-start\">§38</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-start\"></span>)</span>.</p>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-chemical-start\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§38</p><p>A siren wails for 2 minutes – the general warning. You notice a pungent smell, and the wind is blowing from the water-treatment plant.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-inside\">Go straight into the nearest building – the shop opposite the playground → turn to §44</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-inside\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-run\">Run home – it is only 15 minutes → turn to §46</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-run\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-chemical-cellar\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§39</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> After a while the smell in the cellar gets stronger – chlorine is heavier than air and sinks. You hurry upstairs.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 With chlorine and other heavy gases, go to an upper floor, not the cellar. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/chemicka/chemicka-budova\">→ Ch. 19 › In a building<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"chemicka-budova\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-seal\">Turn to §47</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-seal\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-chemical-afterbad\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§40</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> During the night your son is still coughing and his eyes sting. In the morning you have to see a doctor.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 After exposure, wash, launder your clothes and see a doctor if there is coughing or shortness of breath. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/chemicka/chemicka-zasiahnuty\">→ Ch. 19 › If you have been exposed<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"chemicka-zasiahnuty\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-end\">Turn to §53</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-end\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-chemical-up\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§41</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> The air upstairs is cleaner – chlorine stays close to the ground.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-seal\">Turn to §47</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-seal\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-chemical-clear\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§42</p><p>Two hours later the all-clear is given.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-afterok\">Air the rooms, shower at home, wash your clothes and call a doctor if the coughing continues → turn to §49</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-afterok\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-afterbad\">Do nothing special – everything is fine now → turn to §40</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-afterbad\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-chemical-sealok\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§43</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> Hardly any smell gets into the room. The radio says firefighters are stopping the leak.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-school\">Turn to §48</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-school\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-chemical-inside\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§44</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> The shop assistant locks the door, and you are inside with the other customers.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-floor\">Turn to §52</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-floor\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-chemical-window\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§45</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> The smell pours in and everyone starts coughing. You shut the window quickly.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 During a release: windows and doors shut, ventilation off, gaps sealed. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/ukrytie/ukrytie-vnutri\">→ Ch. 6 › Staying inside and sealing a room<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"ukrytie-vnutri\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-school\">Turn to §48</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-school\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-chemical-run\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§46</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> After five minutes your eyes are burning and your son is coughing. The smell is getting stronger, so you dash into the first open doorway.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 During a chemical release go into the nearest building – it does not have to be yours. You are most at risk outdoors. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/chemicka/chemicka-vonku\">→ Ch. 19 › If you are outdoors<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"chemicka-vonku\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-floor\">Turn to §52</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-floor\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-chemical-seal\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§47</p><p>What do you do in the room?</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-sealok\">Close windows and doors, switch off the ventilation, seal the gaps with wet towels and turn on the radio → turn to §43</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-sealok\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-window\">Open a window to see what is happening outside → turn to §45</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-window\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-chemical-school\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§48</p><p>Your partner calls: your daughter's school is two kilometres away and he wants to drive over to pick her up.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-schoolok\">Tell him not to go – the school has a plan and will shelter the children → turn to §50</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-schoolok\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-schoolbad\">Agree that he should fetch her as soon as possible → turn to §51</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-schoolbad\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-chemical-afterok\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§49</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> The cough has eased by evening. A doctor on the phone confirms nothing more is needed.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-end\">Turn to §53</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-end\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-chemical-schoolok\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§50</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> The school sends a message: the children are sheltering in the upstairs gym and are fine.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-clear\">Turn to §42</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-clear\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-chemical-schoolbad\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§51</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> Your partner gets stuck in a queue at a police roadblock, surrounded by the smell, his eyes burning. Meanwhile the school has sheltered the children safely.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Leave children at school unless the authorities say otherwise – the school will shelter them. Travelling would put you in danger. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/varovanie\">→ Ch. 2 · Warnings, information and communication<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"varovanie\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-clear\">Turn to §42</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-clear\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-chemical-floor\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§52</p><p>The radio reports a chlorine leak. The building has a cellar and a first floor.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-up\">Suggest going upstairs to a room on the side facing away from the plant → turn to §41</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-up\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-chemical-cellar\">Suggest hiding in the cellar – surely the safest place → turn to §39</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-chemical-cellar\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node end\" id=\"gb-chemical-end\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§53</p><p>That evening you look up which nearby plants have emergency plans, and you put plastic sheeting and tape ready at home to seal one room.</p><p class=\"gb-end\"><strong>The end.</strong> Count the ✔ marks on your path. Each ✖ shows something worth improving – its tip sends you to the right chapter.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"gb-prepare\"><p><strong>What to prepare in advance</strong></p><ul class=\"checklist\"><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> Know what the siren sounds like and what to do</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> Plastic sheeting, tape and towels to seal a room</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> A battery radio</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> The poison centre number</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> Knowing which nearby plants handle hazardous substances</li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"scenario\" data-scenario=\"fire\">\n<h2 id=\"scenar-fire\">🔥 Fire at night</h2>\n<p class=\"sc-setting\">It is 3 am. You are asleep with your family in a 4th-floor flat in a tower block. The smoke alarm wakes you.</p>\n<div class=\"sc-player no-print\" data-player=\"fire\"></div>\n<div class=\"gamebook\" data-gamebook=\"fire\">\n<p class=\"gb-start\">📖 Paper gamebook (numbered sections): The story starts at <a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-start\">§54</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-start\"></span>)</span>.</p>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-fire-start\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§54</p><p>The alarm is beeping and you can smell smoke in the hall. It seems to be coming from behind the front door – from the stairwell.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-check\">Wake the family and test the front door with the back of your hand to see if it is hot → turn to §58</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-check\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-open\">Quickly open the door to see what is happening → turn to §55</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-open\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-fire-open\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§55</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> Thick black smoke pours in. You slam the door, coughing, and the hall is full of smoke up to the ceiling.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Check the door with the back of your hand before opening it. Never open a hot door – smoke kills faster than fire. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/poziare/poziare-vediet\">→ Ch. 12 › What you need to know<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"poziare-vediet\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-trapped\">Turn to §63</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-trapped\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-fire-callok\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§56</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> The operator notes everything and tells you to stay in the room and signal from the window.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-wait\">Turn to §68</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-wait\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-fire-room\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§57</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> The air in the room with the sealed door is clean.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-call\">Turn to §65</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-call\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-fire-check\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§58</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> The door is hot and smoke is seeping underneath. The stairwell is full of smoke – you keep the door shut.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-trapped\">Turn to §63</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-trapped\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-fire-count\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§59</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> The firefighters find your neighbour and bring her out. Everyone is safe.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-end\">Turn to §69</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-end\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-fire-climb\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§60</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> Your foot slips on the railing and you catch yourself at the last moment. You climb back into the room with grazed hands.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Do not jump or climb from a height. Unless danger is immediate, wait for the firefighters. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/poziare/poziare-uviaznuty\">→ Ch. 12 › If you cannot get out<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"poziare-uviaznuty\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-outside\">Turn to §67</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-outside\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-fire-callbad\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§61</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> The operator has to ask several times exactly where you are. Precious minutes are lost.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Say who is calling, exactly where (address, floor, flat), what is happening and how many people need help. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/varovanie/varovanie-112\">→ Ch. 2 › How to call the emergency line<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"varovanie-112\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-wait\">Turn to §68</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-wait\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-fire-waitok\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§62</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> The firefighters see you, and ten minutes later they lead you down the stairs wearing masks.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-outside\">Turn to §67</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-outside\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-fire-trapped\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§63</p><p>You cannot get out through the stairwell. What do you do?</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-room\">Everyone goes into a room with a window onto the street; you close the door and block the gaps with wet towels → turn to §57</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-room\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-stairs\">Try to run down the stairs holding your breath → turn to §64</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-stairs\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-fire-stairs\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§64</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> Two floors down you cannot see a thing and the smoke burns your lungs. You barely make it back and shut yourselves in a room with a window.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Never enter a smoke-filled stairwell. Stay in a room with a window, seal the door and call 112. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/poziare/poziare-uviaznuty\">→ Ch. 12 › If you cannot get out<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"poziare-uviaznuty\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-call\">Turn to §65</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-call\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-fire-call\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§65</p><p>You call 112. What do you tell the operator first?</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-callok\">The exact address, floor, flat number and how many of you are in a room with a street window → turn to §56</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-callok\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-callbad\">That there is a fire and they must come quickly → turn to §61</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-callbad\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-fire-back\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§66</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> A firefighter stops you at the entrance. An hour later a firefighter carries the cat out – alive.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Never go back into a burning building. Tell the firefighters who or what is still inside. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/poziare/poziare-budova\">→ Ch. 12 › During a fire in a building<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"poziare-budova\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-end\">Turn to §69</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-end\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-fire-outside\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§67</p><p>Neighbours are standing outside in their pyjamas.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-count\">Count your family at the meeting point and tell the firefighters that the lady next door lives alone → turn to §59</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-count\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-back\">Go back into the flat for your documents and the cat → turn to §66</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-back\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-fire-wait\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§68</p><p>The fire brigade is arriving. Smoke is starting to creep under the bedroom door.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-waitok\">Add another wet towel, shine your torch from the window and wait → turn to §62</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-waitok\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-fire-climb\">Try to climb down the balconies to a lower floor → turn to §60</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-fire-climb\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node end\" id=\"gb-fire-end\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§69</p><p>The fire started from an e-scooter charging in the corridor. The next day you buy a fire blanket and a second smoke alarm for the children's room.</p><p class=\"gb-end\"><strong>The end.</strong> Count the ✔ marks on your path. Each ✖ shows something worth improving – its tip sends you to the right chapter.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"gb-prepare\"><p><strong>What to prepare in advance</strong></p><ul class=\"checklist\"><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> A smoke alarm in the hallway</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> A fire extinguisher and fire blanket</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> An agreed meeting point outside the building</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> A torch by the bed</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> Knowing how to seal a door with wet towels</li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"scenario\" data-scenario=\"heat\">\n<h2 id=\"scenar-heat\">🌡️ A week-long heatwave</h2>\n<p class=\"sc-setting\">July, the fifth day above 35 °C. You have a one-year-old, and your 79-year-old father lives alone in an attic flat in town.</p>\n<div class=\"sc-player no-print\" data-player=\"heat\"></div>\n<div class=\"gamebook\" data-gamebook=\"heat\">\n<p class=\"gb-start\">📖 Paper gamebook (numbered sections): The story starts at <a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-heat-start\">§70</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-heat-start\"></span>)</span>.</p>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-heat-start\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§70</p><p>In the morning it is 29 °C in your flat. Yesterday your father said on the phone that he was &quot;fine&quot;.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-heat-visit\">Arrange two phone calls a day with your father and visit him at lunchtime → turn to §74</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-heat-visit\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-heat-nocheck\">Your father is an adult; he will call if he needs anything → turn to §72</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-heat-nocheck\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-heat-flatbad\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§71</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> Hot air streams in through the open windows and the flat heats up to 35 °C.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Keep windows closed and shaded from outside during the day; ventilate at night and early in the morning. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/horucavy/horucavy-pocas\">→ Ch. 10 › During a heatwave<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"horucavy-pocas\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-heat-car\">Turn to §78</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-heat-car\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-heat-nocheck\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§72</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> In the evening your father does not answer the phone. When you arrive he is confused and his skin is hot and red.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Older people often do not feel thirst or heat. Check on them at least twice a day during a heatwave. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/zranitelni/zranitelni-seniori\">→ Ch. 25 › Older people<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"zranitelni-seniori\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-heat-stroke\">Turn to §79</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-heat-stroke\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-heat-strokebad\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§73</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> Your father gets worse and loses consciousness. The ambulance takes him to intensive care.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Heatstroke is life-threatening: call 112 and cool aggressively. Fever medicine does not help with heatstroke. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/horucavy/horucavy-priznaky\">→ Ch. 10 › How to recognise overheating<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"horucavy-priznaky\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-heat-end\">Turn to §83</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-heat-end\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-heat-visit\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§74</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> At lunchtime you find your father in a flat at 33 °C. He is tired but talking normally. He has drunk only one glass of water all morning.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-heat-flat\">Turn to §75</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-heat-flat\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-heat-flat\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§75</p><p>How do you help him with the flat?</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-heat-flatok\">Shade the windows from outside during the day, air the flat at night, give him a fan and keep a bottle of water within reach with a drinking schedule → turn to §81</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-heat-flatok\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-heat-flatbad\">Open all the windows wide for a through-draught, even during the day → turn to §71</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-heat-flatbad\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-heat-carbad\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§76</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> There is a queue at the till. After twelve minutes it is 47 °C in the car and the baby is drenched in sweat and crying. You cool them down quickly and give them a drink.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Never leave a child, an older person or an animal in a car – the temperature rises by more than 10 °C in 10 minutes. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/horucavy/horucavy-pocas\">→ Ch. 10 › During a heatwave<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"horucavy-pocas\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-heat-evening\">Turn to §77</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-heat-evening\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-heat-evening\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§77</p><p>In the evening your father sounds confused on the phone and does not know what day it is. You go to him at once.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-heat-stroke\">Turn to §79</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-heat-stroke\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-heat-car\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§78</p><p>In the afternoon you go shopping with the baby, who falls asleep in the car. The shopping will take five minutes.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-heat-carok\">Wake the baby and take them with you → turn to §80</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-heat-carok\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-heat-carbad\">Let the baby sleep in the car with the window open a crack → turn to §76</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-heat-carbad\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-heat-stroke\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§79</p><p>Your father is confused, his skin is hot and dry, and he refuses to drink. What do you do?</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-heat-strokeok\">Call 112, undress him, cool him with wet sheets and a fan, and put ice on his neck and groin → turn to §82</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-heat-strokeok\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-heat-strokebad\">Give him a fever tablet and let him sleep it off → turn to §73</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-heat-strokebad\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-heat-carok\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§80</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> The baby is grumpy, but the shop is air-conditioned and you manage the shopping together.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-heat-evening\">Turn to §77</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-heat-evening\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-heat-flatok\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§81</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> By evening the flat is at 30 °C and it drops to 26 °C overnight. Your father is drinking to schedule.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-heat-car\">Turn to §78</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-heat-car\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-heat-strokeok\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§82</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> The paramedics are glad you started cooling him straight away. They take him in for observation, and the next day he is better.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-heat-end\">Turn to §83</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-heat-end\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node end\" id=\"gb-heat-end\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§83</p><p>Until the heatwave ends your father stays in your cooler flat. You buy him external shading and a thermometer with large numbers.</p><p class=\"gb-end\"><strong>The end.</strong> Count the ✔ marks on your path. Each ✖ shows something worth improving – its tip sends you to the right chapter.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"gb-prepare\"><p><strong>What to prepare in advance</strong></p><ul class=\"checklist\"><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> External shading or reflective film for windows</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> An indoor thermometer</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> A plan for daily contact with older relatives</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> Oral rehydration salts</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> Knowing how to recognise heatstroke and what to do</li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"scenario\" data-scenario=\"war\">\n<h2 id=\"scenar-war\">🛡️ Air-raid alert at 2 am</h2>\n<p class=\"sc-setting\">You live in a city flat with your partner and 10-year-old son. In the night a siren and a phone alert wake you: &quot;Air-raid alert – take shelter immediately.&quot;</p>\n<div class=\"sc-player no-print\" data-player=\"war\"></div>\n<div class=\"gamebook\" data-gamebook=\"war\">\n<p class=\"gb-start\">📖 Paper gamebook (numbered sections): The story starts at <a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-start\">§84</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-start\"></span>)</span>.</p>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-war-start\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§84</p><p>The siren is wailing and your phone is buzzing. The nearest public shelter is an underground car park three minutes from your building.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-go\">Grab the shelter bag and go straight to the car park → turn to §85</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-go\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-window\">First look out of the window to see if anything is visible → turn to §89</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-window\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-war-go\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§85</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> Three minutes later you are in the car park with other neighbours. You have water, torches, medicines and blankets.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-shelter\">Turn to §92</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-shelter\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-war-fake\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§86</p><p>In the morning a message arrives from an unknown number: &quot;The government has ordered the whole city to evacuate – head for the border now!&quot;</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-verify\">Check it on the radio and on the interior ministry's and municipality's websites → turn to §94</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-verify\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-share\">Forward it to your family straight away and start packing → turn to §88</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-share\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-war-debris\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§87</p><p>On the way to the shop you see a metal fragment with wires lying in the grass.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-debrisok\">Do not touch it; mark the spot, warn passers-by and call 112 → turn to §91</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-debrisok\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-debrisbad\">Take a close-up photo and carry it to the police station → turn to §90</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-debrisbad\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-war-share\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§88</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> Traffic jams build up on the roads out of the city. An hour later the radio announces that the message was fake and no evacuation has been ordered.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Disinformation spreads in a crisis. Check the source and share nothing until the authorities confirm it. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/varovanie/varovanie-dezinformacie\">→ Ch. 2 › How to check information and resist disinformation<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"varovanie-dezinformacie\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-debris\">Turn to §87</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-debris\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-war-window\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§89</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> You lose two minutes at the window and see nothing. Had something landed nearby, the glass itself would have been the greatest danger.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 When the alarm sounds, do not wait and keep away from windows – flying glass causes the most injuries. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/konflikt/konflikt-utok\">→ Ch. 20 › During an air attack<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"konflikt-utok\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-late\">Turn to §95</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-late\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-war-debrisbad\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§90</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> The police officer is alarmed: it could have been an unexploded part of a drone. You were lucky.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Never touch suspicious objects. Move away, mark the spot and call 112. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/konflikt/konflikt-municia\">→ Ch. 20 › Unexploded ordnance<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"konflikt-municia\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-end\">Turn to §99</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-end\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-war-debrisok\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§91</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> Bomb-disposal experts arrive within the hour and safely remove the fragment – part of a drone, still carrying explosives.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-end\">Turn to §99</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-end\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-war-shelter\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§92</p><p>A neighbour is filming an impact site visible through the car-park entrance and wants to post the video.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-filmok\">Ask him not to post anything → turn to §93</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-filmok\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-filmbad\">Let him – people have a right to know what is happening → turn to §97</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-filmbad\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-war-filmok\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§93</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> The neighbour deletes the video and the others agree with you.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-fake\">Turn to §86</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-fake\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-war-verify\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§94</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> The radio confirms it is disinformation. You stay at home and follow official instructions.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-debris\">Turn to §87</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-debris\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node\" id=\"gb-war-late\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§95</p><p>You can hear explosions in the distance. The car park is three minutes away along the street.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-twowall\">Stay in the flat in the hallway behind two walls, away from windows → turn to §98</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-twowall\"></span>)</span></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-street\">Run along the street to the car park → turn to §96</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-street\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-war-street\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§96</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> The street is dark and a shop window has shattered. You reach the car park, but your son cuts his hand on the glass.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 If you cannot reach a shelter within a few minutes, use the two-wall rule inside your building. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/ukrytie/ukrytie-dve-steny\">→ Ch. 6 › The two-wall rule<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"ukrytie-dve-steny\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-shelter\">Turn to §92</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-shelter\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node bad\" id=\"gb-war-filmbad\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§97</p><p><span class=\"gb-v bad\">✖ Risky decision.</span> The video spreads online with its exact location. The authorities later warn that such footage helps the attacker aim further strikes.</p><p class=\"gb-tip\">💡 Do not photograph or post impact sites, troop movements or shelter locations. <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#/kniha/konflikt/konflikt-utok\">→ Ch. 20 › During an air attack<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"konflikt-utok\"></span></a></p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-fake\">Turn to §86</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-fake\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node good\" id=\"gb-war-twowall\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§98</p><p><span class=\"gb-v good\">✔ Good decision.</span> You sit on the floor of the hallway with two walls between you and the street. The battery radio gives further instructions.</p><ul class=\"gb-choices\"><li><a href=\"#/kniha/scenare/gb-war-shelter\">Turn to §92</a><span class=\"pref same\"> (→ <span class=\"pg\" data-id=\"gb-war-shelter\"></span>)</span></li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"gb-node end\" id=\"gb-war-end\"><p class=\"gb-num\">§99</p><p>In the evening you go over with your family where the shelter is, which spot in the flat meets the two-wall rule and what belongs in the shelter bag.</p><p class=\"gb-end\"><strong>The end.</strong> Count the ✔ marks on your path. Each ✖ shows something worth improving – its tip sends you to the right chapter.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"gb-prepare\"><p><strong>What to prepare in advance</strong></p><ul class=\"checklist\"><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> Know where the nearest shelter is and how long it takes to get there</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> A shelter bag: water, light, medicines, documents</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> A spot in the flat chosen in advance using the two-wall rule</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> A battery radio</li><li><span class=\"cb\" aria-hidden=\"true\">☐</span> Trusted sources of information</li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<h2 id=\"scenare-dalej\">Where next</h2>\n<nav class=\"choices\" id=\"volba-scenare-1\" aria-label=\"Your choice\"><p class=\"choices-label\">🎲 Your choice</p><ul><li><a href=\"#/kniha/kontrolne-zoznamy\"><span class=\"ch-t\">Prepare based on your result</span><span class=\"xr\">Ch. 30 · Checklists<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"kontrolne-zoznamy\"></span></span></a></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/nakupne-zoznamy\"><span class=\"ch-t\">Top up your supplies</span><span class=\"xr\">Ch. 28 · Food shopping lists for 3, 7, 14 and 30 days<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"nakupne-zoznamy\"></span></span></a></li><li><a href=\"#/kniha/plan\"><span class=\"ch-t\">Agree with your family</span><span class=\"xr\">Ch. 3 · Family emergency plan<span class=\"ch-page\" data-id=\"plan\"></span></span></a></li></ul></nav>\n");
